(3) T(2^k) = 1/(k+1) exactly when k+1 is a power of 2 (checked k+1 = 1,2,4,...,128)
(1) brute force: W(y)*2^n versus T(n) (programs <N>w with N <= 14 enumerated, rest analytic)
    n=1: for all 2 label strings y, W(y)*2^n = T(n) = 1.000000 (extra -0.000 bits; len_delta(n) = 1)
    n=2: for all 4 label strings y, W(y)*2^n = T(n) = 0.500000 (extra 1.000 bits; len_delta(n) = 4)
    n=3: for all 8 label strings y, W(y)*2^n = T(n) = 0.437500 (extra 1.193 bits; len_delta(n) = 4)
    n=4: for all 16 label strings y, W(y)*2^n = T(n) = 0.375000 (extra 1.415 bits; len_delta(n) = 5)
    n=5: for all 32 label strings y, W(y)*2^n = T(n) = 0.343750 (extra 1.541 bits; len_delta(n) = 5)
    n=6: for all 64 label strings y, W(y)*2^n = T(n) = 0.312500 (extra 1.678 bits; len_delta(n) = 5)
(2) extra cost of the program mixture (-log2 T(n)) versus the cost of encoding n (len_delta(n)):
   n              -log2 T(n)   len_delta(n)   log2(log2 n + 1)
   2^4                 2.193            9        2.322
   2^4+3               2.232            9        2.392
   3*2^2+1             2.117            8        2.233
   2^8                 3.093           15        3.170
   2^8+3               3.094           15        3.173
   3*2^6+1             3.047           14        3.103
   2^16                4.046           25        4.087
   2^16+3              4.046           25        4.087
   3*2^14+1            4.023           24        4.052
   2^32                5.023           43        5.044
   2^32+12345          5.023           43        5.044
   3*2^30+1            5.011           42        5.026
   2^64                6.011           77        6.022
   2^64+12345          6.011           77        6.022
   3*2^62+1            6.006           76        6.013
   2^128               7.006          143        7.011
   2^128+12345         7.006          143        7.011
   3*2^126+1           7.003          142        7.007
   2^200               7.484          215        7.651
   2^200+12345         7.484          215        7.651
   3*2^198+1           7.480          214        7.648
RESULT: in the toy language the mixture's extra cost over 2^-n is -log2 T(n) <= log2(log2 n + 1) + 2,
        while encoding n costs len_delta(n) ~ log2 n + 2 log2 log2 n.  Since K(N) <= len_delta(N) + c,
        the real W_hist pays at most -log2 T(n) + c extra on every label string: not ~K(n).
